+
+## 🎯 Project Overview
+
+Pulseboard is a small web product for team facilitators who lose action items after weekly meetings. A facilitator uploads a meeting transcript, reviews proposed action items extracted from it, and must confirm an owner and due date before a reminder can be scheduled. The five-team pilot tests whether this narrow, human-confirmed workflow prevents commitments from disappearing without replacing existing meeting, calendar, or messaging tools.
+
+## 🎨 Project Type & Scale
+
+**Type**: Web Application (browser-based, responsive)  
+**Estimated Scale**: Level 2 — moderate feature set, likely one to two epics after planning.  
+**Primary Domain**: Enterprise/B2B — team meeting follow-through.  
+**Project Archetype**: `b2b_saas`  
+**Domain Expertise Required**: No specialized regulated domain is indicated. Transcript privacy, retention, and participant-consent needs require clarification before pilot data is handled.
+
+## 🚀 Vision & Goals
+
+### Vision Statement
+
+A world where team facilitators can turn weekly meeting discussion into owned, time-bound follow-through so that important actions do not disappear after the call.
+
+### Primary Goals
+
+1. **Review completion**: at least 80% of proposed action items are reviewed during the five-team pilot.
+   - Success looks like: facilitators explicitly decide the majority of extracted proposals.
+   - Key metric: reviewed proposed items ÷ all proposed items.
+2. **Action accountability**: reduce unowned overdue actions by 30% after four weeks.
+   - Success looks like: fewer overdue actions lack a named owner than at pilot baseline.
+   - Key metric: count of overdue actions without an owner, compared with baseline.
+3. **Human confirmation before outreach**: no reminder can be scheduled without a confirmed owner and due date.
+   - Success looks like: every schedulable reminder has both fields confirmed by the facilitator.
+   - Key metric: reminders scheduled without both confirmations; target 0.
+
