+
+## 🎯 Jobs-to-Be-Done (JTBD)
+
+### Core Functional Job
+
+**Primary Job Statement**: Convert a weekly-meeting transcript into confirmed, owned, due-dated action items.
+
+**Job Context**: When a weekly meeting ends and a transcript is available; with the transcript, facilitator judgment, and participants; the goal is a trustworthy action list that can be reminded on later.
+
+### Related Jobs
+
+1. **Triage proposed actions**: decide whether an extracted proposal is a real commitment. Relationship: during the core job.
+2. **Follow up on confirmed commitments**: remind an owner when a confirmed action needs attention. Relationship: after the core job.
+
+### Emotional & Social Jobs
+
+**Emotional Jobs**: facilitators want confidence that commitments were not lost and relief from manually chasing every action.  
+**Social Jobs**: facilitators want to appear organized and fair, not as people who assign work or send messages without a confirmed basis.
+
+### Key Desired Outcomes (Ranked)
+
+| Priority | Outcome Statement | Current Pain Level |
+|----------|-------------------|--------------------|
+| 1 | Minimize the likelihood that a genuine meeting action has no confirmed owner | High |
+| 2 | Minimize time required to review proposed actions after a weekly meeting | High |
+| 3 | Minimize the likelihood of scheduling a reminder without a due date | High |
+| 4 | Reduce overdue actions that remain unowned | High |
+| 5 | Increase facilitator confidence in transcript-derived action lists | Medium |
+
+### Competitive Job Executors
+
+| Current Solution | Strengths | Weaknesses (Opportunities) |
+|------------------|-----------|-----------------------------|
+| Personal meeting notes | Flexible and familiar | Actions can be omitted, unowned, or invisible |
+| Manual task-list entry | Creates explicit tasks | Duplicates transcript review and follow-up work |
+| Informal facilitator follow-up | Preserves human context | Inconsistent, time-consuming, and hard to measure |
+
+### JTBD-Driven Prioritization
+
+Prioritize high-pain, low-reliability outcomes: review proposed actions, confirm owner and due date, then permit reminder scheduling.
+
+## 📊 Success Metrics
+
+### Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
+
+**Business Metrics**: five participating teams complete the pilot; measured by pilot roster and active use records.  
+**User Metrics**: proposed-item review rate of at least 80%; measured as reviewed items divided by all proposed items. Unowned overdue actions fall 30% after four weeks; measured against a baseline. The clarification phase must define the baseline observation window and current source of record.  
+**Product-Safety Metric**: zero reminders scheduled without facilitator-confirmed owner and due date; measured from scheduling records.
+
+### Project Definition of Done
+
+- [ ] Facilitators can upload a transcript and review proposed actions.
+- [ ] The product prevents reminder scheduling until owner and due date are confirmed.
+- [ ] Five teams can participate in the pilot.
+- [ ] Review-rate and unowned-overdue metrics are measurable.
+- [ ] The pilot outcome can be assessed after four weeks.
