+## 🏗️ High-Level Scope
+
+### Core Capabilities (v1)
+
+**Transcript-based action proposals**: accept an uploaded transcript and present proposed action items. Critical because the pilot starts with meeting discussion otherwise lost in an unstructured record; value is reduced discovery work while preserving human judgment.
+
+**Facilitator confirmation workflow**: review proposals and explicitly confirm owner and due date. Critical because confirmation is the trust boundary; value is accountability before follow-up.
+
+**Guarded reminder scheduling**: allow scheduling only after owner and due date are confirmed. Critical because it enforces the safety requirement; value is follow-through without guessing intent or responsibility.
+
+**Pilot measurement**: measure item review and unowned overdue actions. Critical because these decide whether the pilot worked; value is evidence rather than anecdotes.
+
+### Future Capabilities (v2+)
+
+**Reminder delivery-channel integration**: email or Slack delivery after a channel is selected. Deferred because the brief leaves it undecided; prerequisites are channel, recipient/consent rules, and a non-autonomous sending boundary.
+
+**Broader meeting and task management**: recording, calendar replacement, or general task management. Deferred because each dilutes the accountability pilot; each needs separate evidence and scope approval.
+
+### Explicit Out of Scope
+
+- Meeting recording — Pulseboard consumes uploaded transcripts.
+- Calendar replacement — existing calendars remain the scheduling source.
+- Autonomous message sending — it must not independently send messages based only on extraction.
+- Treating a proposed action as real without facilitator review.
+
